on of the pancreatic duct was eliminated by bromhexine hydrochloride</article-title><source>Intern Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>1034</fpage><lpage>1038</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15609697</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2169/internalmedicine.43.1034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bhasin</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><name><surname>Rana</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Chandail</surname><given-names>VS</given-names></name><name><surname>Nanda</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinha</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Nagi</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Successful resolution of a mediastinal pseudocyst and pancreatic pleural effusion by endoscopic nasopancreatic drainage</article-title><source>JOP</source><year>2005</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>359</fpage><lpage>364</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16006688</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bardia</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Stoikes</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>NW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mediastinal pancreatic pseudocyst with acute airway obstruction</article-title><source>J Gastrointest Surg</source><year>2006</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>146</fpage><lpage>150</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16368505</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.gassur.2005.05.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sadat</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Jah</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Huguet</surname><given